## Awards & Recognition

Freycinet Vineyard has received accolades from national wine shows. The winery is recognized as one of Australia's foremost producers of Pinot Noir and Chardonnay. Their Riesling and traditional method sparkling wines have also garnered acclaim. Recent specific awards for the 2025 Freycinet Riesling include a Gold at the 2025 WINEWISE CHAMPIONSHIP, 95/100 Elite at the Canberra International Riesling Challenge, the Best Riesling - Cool Wine Trophy at the 2026 Tasmanian Wine Show, and the WINEWISE BEST 2024/2025 RIESLING - TROPHY. The winery's wines have been reviewed by critics such as Dave Brookes for Halliday Wine Companion. Specific scores include 96 points for the 2016 Freycinet Radenti Grand Vintage Sparkling, 94 points for the 2019 Freycinet Cabernet Sauvignon Merlot and the 2025 Freycinet Riesling, 93 points for the 2024 Freycinet Chardonnay, 92 points for the Freycinet Wineglass Bay Sauvignon Blanc 2025, and 91 points for the 2024 Freycinet Louis Chardonnay and Freycinet Louis Pinot Noir 2025.

